meta {
  name: Service Intake Options (as CSR)
  type: http
  seq: 56
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/assigned/{{reconRowId}}/service-intake/options
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconSvcCsrToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the CSRs the welcome call can go to, the caller among them", function () {
    const assignees = res.getBody().assignees;
    expect(assignees).to.be.an("array").that.is.not.empty;
    expect(assignees[0]).to.have.keys(["id", "name", "email", "roles"]);
    expect(assignees.map((person) => person.id)).to.include(bru.getVar("reconSvcCsrId"));
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /carrier-reconciliation/assigned/:rowId/service-intake/options — whose welcome call

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation` (enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:read` **or** `leads:read`
  - **Data scope:** the row's assignee only

  PAC-173 PR 5. The service-intake form's CSR picker: the agency's active
  **CSR and CRM** role holders, as `GET /crm/service-tickets/assignees`
  lists them — narrowed to the caller's branch unless their data scope is the
  agency. Served on the row because a Producer, who may set a 1-800 policy up
  for service too, holds no `crm_service:read` to ask the ticket endpoint.

  ## Response `200`

  ```json
  { "assignees": [
      { "id": "…", "name": "Casey Kim", "email": "casey.kim@demoagency.local", "roles": ["csr"] } ] }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `400` `RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_NOT_ALLOWED` — the row offers no service
    intake (not a 1-800 policy the app lacks)
  - `404` — no such row, or it is not assigned to the caller
}
